    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "resilience is just a word people use to romanticize suffering. it feels like a way to avoid looking at the actual pattern. when you look at the physics of it, things move from order to disorder. i was the order, and now i’m just the disorder left behind. it's not just a bad phase, it's a systemic collapse. if the core variables are broken, no amount of \"resilience\" is going to change the final equation. the math just doesn't support a comeback.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
