      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I understand that relying on \"resilience\" feels dismissive when you believe you have identified a hard, unchangeable system failure in your life.\n\nPlease take a moment to consider that while the company is gone, the \"order\" you once built—your knowledge, empathy, and the lives you helped—existed for real and do not vanish with the collapse.\n\nThis feeling of inevitable decay might be a natural psychological defense against the pain of loss, even if the \"math\" you are seeing doesn't support a comeback.",
